comments.body:
Yeah, I guess that was a little bit confusing.

I'm customizing `__init__` in a way that would break if functions like `model_validate()` would call it (taking one argument, as a positional one). It made sense to me, as this is pretty similar to what SQLAlchemy is doing with models (you can use `__init__` to construct objects, but when data is read from database, `__init__` is not called).

@sydney-runkle said that it seemed like a bug, so I pointed out that it may be used as a feature as well by some folks.

@aguckenber-chwy as for your case, maybe overriding `model_post_init` is what you need?
